 Claude guides through all six stages, stopping at each boundary.
+
+## Delivery metrics
+
+Each ticket keeps `impl/stat.json` alongside `2-report.md`. Context initializes it;
+every stage records observed work and waits, and Implement updates per-step metrics
+before verification waits and after confirmed outcomes. The router finalizes completed
+lead/cycle times after required completion work; Document preserves the file through archival. Direct-stage runs mark
+partial coverage; interruptions do not count automatically as active work.
+
+Lead time runs from the known tracker creation timestamp to lifecycle completion;
+cycle time runs from the first observed lifecycle work to completion. Human effort is
+reported separately. Runtime input/output token usage is recorded only when exposed,
+with source and coverage; unavailable measurements stay null. The report summarizes
+per-step timing, attempts and failed checks from the JSON rather than inventing totals.
+
+The portable dev skill includes `scripts/dev-metrics.mjs` (Node.js, no dependencies).
+It owns timestamping, validated transitions, atomic JSON writes, command verification
+capture, recovery checkpoints, and report rendering. Every call requires an explicit
+ticket impl directory. See the dev skill's `patterns/metrics.md` for commands and
+`templates/stat.schema.json` for the versioned interface. Only runtime-provided token
+deltas are accepted; no token usage or human effort is inferred.
